2. Permitted use of this repository

Subject to the licenses above, you may:

  (a) fork, clone and run the generator, and use this repository as the
      engine for your own GitHub profile;
  (b) adapt, extend and redistribute the Software, including for
      commercial purposes, under the MIT License;
  (c) change the theme, colors, layout, locales and styles of your own
      profile by editing configuration files and templates;
  (d) share the Creative Works verbatim and unmodified, for
      non-commercial purposes only, with the attribution in Section 5.


3. Prompts

The text of the generation prompts in
assets/profile/backgrounds/prompts/, and the banner prompt reproduced in
docs/design.md, is licensed under the MIT License. It is published as a
reference so that you can generate your own, independent artwork.

The license of the prompts does not extend to the image files in this
repository. The images generated from these prompts remain Creative
Works under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, and nothing in this Section grants any right
in them.


4. Template Usage Clause

This Section states the consequences of the licenses in Section 1 for a
person who forks or copies this repository as the basis for a profile of
their own (a "Derived Profile"). It grants no right beyond those licenses
and imposes no restriction on the Software.

A Derived Profile may use the Software under the MIT License. Before a
Derived Profile is published, the following must be replaced with your
own material, because the license of the Creative Works does not permit
their use there:

  (a) the image files assets/profile/banner.webp and
      assets/profile/backgrounds/**/*.webp, and every generated file that
      embeds them (assets/generated/ and the generated READMEs);
  (b) the texts in locales/readme/*/strings.json that describe the
      Licensor, the Licensor's projects and interests, and the banner;
  (c) the identity, contact, project and catalog entries in
      configs/profile.json, and the data in configs/data/snapshot.json;
  (d) the name, account, e-mail address, messenger handle and links that
      identify the Licensor or any other natural person.

A Derived Profile must not:

  (i)   use the original banner or panel backgrounds, whether unchanged
        or edited, because CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 grants no right to create or
        share adaptations;
  (ii)  retain, display or publish personal data of the Licensor or of
        any other person that is contained in this repository;
  (iii) reproduce the Creative Works, in whole or in substantial part, so
        as to form a copy of the Licensor's profile ("1:1 clone"), or
        present them as the work or identity of anyone other than the
        Licensor.

You are encouraged to change the colors in configs/theme.json, and to
replace the graphics, so that your profile has its own identity. Nothing
in this Section restricts the exercise of rights in the Software under
the MIT License, and no technical measure prevents it.


